jobs_results.description:
Joining Mirabaud, means entering an entrepreneurial and innovative environment. With the 7th generation of the Mirabaud family working within the bank, the culture is that of a family business. With over 750 employees based in 10 countries worldwide, Mirabaud offers opportunities to develop one’s career across an international network of 16 offices.

A day in your future job:
• Designing and implementing automated test cases to improve the efficiency and effectiveness of the testing process;
• Analysing test results and reporting on the status of test automation to quality assurance team and the management, including identifying areas for improvement and implementing changes as necessary;
• Ensuring that the test automation processes comply with industry standards and regulations and that appropriate documentation is maintained;
• Work with the QA team to ensure that all testing is completed on time and meets quality standards;
• Continuously improve testing processes and... methodologies to increase efficiency and effectiveness;
• Define test cases and scenarios for new functionalities;
• Assist business analysts and auditors.

Your assets to succeed:
• At least 3 years of experience in test automation for banking applications;
• Experience in automation mobile and/or desktop or mainframe technologies;
• Excellent understanding and experience with xpath, selenium WebDriver, Cucumber, Java – at least 3 + (or another language), Appium, Git, Azure DevOps;
• Ability to understand and review automated test cases;
• Good technical writing, documentation, and communication skills;
• Rigorous, autonomous, and dynamic with good interpersonal skills, as well as an aptitude for analytical problem solving;
• Degree in computer engineering, business administration, or related field; ISTQB certification is an advantage but not required;
• Capable to work in an English environment with a high capacity to handle stress.

Jump on the boat!
• Family-friendly and dynamic environment;
• Direct impact on the business, no matter your position or seniority;
• Work in an environment that encourages autonomy and entrepreneurship;
• Flexible working arrangements to help you achieve a better work-life balance;
• Variety of cultural and sporting activities during your free time;
• Inclusion and equal treatment;
• Various employee benefits & family friendly benefits.

Apply now: recrutement@mirabaud.com

Notes:
• Please send us your CV in English.
• Only candidates selected for an interview will be contacted. Many thanks for your understanding.
• We will not accept any CVs from agencies

